IPsec Client: whoever talks VICI cannot make charon open files by path
(audit of 0.2.0, P9).

With the options of patch 0001 set (charon.plugins.vici.force_updown or
force_if_id, written by the embedded engine's entrypoint), charon runs as
root on behalf of the session user. VICI lets the client name a certificate
by file path ("file") or by token ("handle") in load-conn (cert/cacert
sections) and load-authority: root charon then opens that path, which tells
the user whether a file exists and is readable by root. In that mode both are
refused; certificates still come as data ("certs", "cacerts", load-cert).
Without those options, upstream behavior is unchanged.

Applies to strongSwan 6.x after patch 0001 (tested on 6.1.0).

--- a/src/libcharon/plugins/vici/vici_config.c
+++ b/src/libcharon/plugins/vici/vici_config.c
@@ -2063,6 +2063,23 @@
 					   &peer->request->reply);
 }
 
+/**
+ * IPsec Client: in the embedded engine (force_updown or force_if_id set,
+ * ADR-0019) charon runs as root, and whoever talks VICI must not make it open
+ * files by path nor use tokens: certificates come as data (audit of 0.2.0,
+ * P9). Without those options, upstream behavior is unchanged.
+ */
+static bool refuse_cred_paths(void)
+{
+	char *updown;
+
+	updown = lib->settings->get_str(lib->settings,
+									"%s.plugins.vici.force_updown", NULL, lib->ns);
+	return (updown && *updown) ||
+		   lib->settings->get_int(lib->settings,
+								  "%s.plugins.vici.force_if_id", 0, lib->ns);
+}
+
